Thank you for reaching out to Pineapple Support, and for choosing us to be a part of your mental wellness journey. <br/><br/>
We are happy to welcome you and inform you that your therapy request has been accepted. Due to the high volume of requests at this time we are experiencing a wait in services. We appreciate your patience while we find an available therapist best suited to your requirements.<br/><br/> 
To provide consistency and support we have on ongoing variety of <a href="https://pineapplesupport.org/support-groups/">support groups</a> that are therapist-led, as well as peer support options. We highly encourage usage of these incredibly helpful resources at this time. <br/><br/>
One of our therapists or counsellors will be in contact, as soon as we have availability, to arrange an assessment session.<br/><br/><br/>

If you would like to take another look at our full Therapy Policies and Procedures, please <a href="https://pineapplesupport.org/therapy-policies-and-procedures/">click here </a>.<br/><br/><br/>


In order for us to carry on helping others, we wanted to remind you of a couple of our <a href="https://pineapplesupport.org/therapy-policies-and-procedures/">Therapy Policies and Procedures;</a><br/><br/><br/>

<b>•      Payment</b> - Pineapple Support does not take any payment for therapy sessions, therefore, your contribution should be paid directly to your therapist before each session.<br/><br/> 

<b>•      No Shows</b> (not turning up for a session without giving your mental health practitioner sufficient notice) – We want to be sure that folks taking part in our therapy programs are receiving care at the time that’s right for them. Therefore, failure to be present for more than two sessions without giving the therapist sufficient notice* will result in the termination of your charitable funding from Pineapple Support. This means a much-needed place can be freed up for one of the folks on our waiting list. Once you are in a situation that allows you to restart your journey, you are welcome to reach out to us and get reconnected to a mental health practitioner.<br/><br/>
Pineapple Support will not pay for any missed or cancelled appointments. At the provider’s discretion and in accordance with the provider’s established practice policy, as discussed with the client during the initial session, providers may bill the client for the entire cost of a missed or cancelled appointment at the applicable rate.<br/><br/>
Clients should be aware that if 3 sessions are missed without giving sufficient notice to their therapist or counselor, Pineapple Support funding will be terminated. <br/><br/><br/>




With love, the Pineapple Support therapy team


